      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand the code before improving it.Now I have a clear picture. The original test has several understandability problems:\n1. Two data-provider methods (`data_valid`, `data_invalid`) that are unused by the single test method — they add noise and imply context that doesn't exist here\n2. Many unused imports clutter the top of the file\n3. No explanation of *why* `assertSame` is the right assertion (i.e., `readResolve()` singleton contract)\n\nI'll write an improved version with those issues fixed.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes the two unused data-provider methods and all unused imports, and adds a brief comment explaining why `assertSame` (reference equality) is the correct assertion — linking it to `Hours.readResolve()` restoring the singleton contract on deserialization."
